  "title": "how a Windows install fails, and where a message could still reach someone",
  "source": "code-read",
  "source_detail": "install.sh:18-38 for what the installer does once running; Claude Code's Windows setup docs for the PowerShell fallback and the settings key that points at Git Bash; Q1 of this plan",
  "explanation": "Two failures, and they are not the same problem: the left one is loud and immediate but arrives with nothing from us attached, and the right one prints success and then breaks something unrelated-looking an hour later. Look at which of [the three catches](#the-catches) can reach each — the README reaches neither, because in both cases the person had no reason to open it. Leaves out what the installer does when it does run, which is unchanged.",
